---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description="Uzi Network privacy policy.">
  <article class="container-x py-12 max-w-3xl prose-blog">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-ink-400 text-sm">Last updated: {new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-US', { month: 'long', day: 'numeric', year: 'numeric' })}</p>

    <p>
      Short version: we collect as little as possible. We never sell your data. We use privacy-respecting analytics.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Email address</strong> — only if you subscribe to the newsletter. Stored by our email service
      provider (currently configured via the <code>EMAIL_PROVIDER</code> env var). We use it to send you the newsletter
      and nothing else.</li>
      <li><strong>Anonymous analytics</strong> — page views, referrers, device type. We use Plausible Analytics
      (or Cloudflare Web Analytics) which are cookieless and GDPR-compliant by default.</li>
      <li><strong>Affiliate click tracking</strong> — when you click an affiliate link, that retailer or network
      sets their own cookies. Read their policies for details.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What we don't do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We don't sell your data. Ever.</li>
      <li>We don't run third-party tracking scripts (no Google Analytics, no Facebook Pixel).</li>
      <li>We don't load ads until we hit traffic thresholds, and even then we'll use cookieless ad networks.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You can unsubscribe from the newsletter at any time using the link at the bottom of any email. You can
      email us to request deletion of any data we hold on you. We respond within 7 days.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>